ause the  the rising power china is going to  challenge  more and more the united states  and the order it's established after the  end of the cold war so this is the  moment of this shifting end of this  negotiation  but  we are not going to see immediate uh uh  an immediate clash of military might  between these two superpowers but  it might eventually come a little bit  later uh just one caveat towards the the  last statement i think that europe went  through a period of peace  after the end of the cold war but during  that period of peace we had the war  there was in bosnia the war in  kosovo we had  georgia we had the first invasion of  ukraine and  crimea so this period was not that  peaceful and that's calm in europe  either so  that was the only uh  slight disagreement i wanted to sure all  right we'll have to leave it there  thanks very much indeed gentlemen for  joining us today nizam asadi glenn  diesen and steve sang thanks very much  indeed for joining us for this  interesting discussion and thank you too  for watching you can see this program  again anytime by visiting our website  aljazeera.com and indeed for further  discussion just go to our facebook page  that's facebook.com forward slash aj  inside story and you can also join the  conversation on twitter our handle is at  aj inside story from mainland clark the  entire team here in doha it's goodbye  for now  you
 

